1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Candy Sticker Generator — a local AI sticker studio powered by AMD ROCm on a single consumer GPU.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Everything runs on an AMD Radeon GPU — RDNA3, 48GB VRAM, ROCm 7.2. No NVIDIA required.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:28,000
At idle the card draws only about 16 watts. Let's put it to work.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Mode 1 — Text to Sticker. Type a prompt plus the style trigger, then hit Generate.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Our custom "stkstyle" LoRA gives every sticker a consistent candy-chibi look.

6
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The model renders a full 8-expression sticker sheet. Watch the GPU power climb as it works.

7
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Peak draw hits around 212 watts while generating — real local inference on AMD hardware.

8
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Each SDXL image takes about 9.4 seconds. Here is the finished 8-expression set.

9
00:01:48,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Mode 2 — Reference Image. Upload a photo and the model re-renders it in the sticker style.

10
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Mode 3 — Sketch. Draw a rough doodle and watch it become a polished chibi sticker.

11
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:40,000
All three modes share the same backend and the same stkstyle LoRA.

12
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:56,000
It is fully self-contained: code, model weights and the LoRA all live in one Git repository.

13
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Thanks for watching. Check the repo for setup instructions and the full source.
